From 043b77b0f88e280eb77d39a000b9fd48bdafbf07 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mikkojhuttunen <mikkojhuttunen@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 16:25:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Cavity workbench: always draw layout and add paraxial ray
 trace

The layout schematic was hidden whenever the cavity was unstable, so
students saw an empty panel exactly when they needed help. Element
positions now come from the gaps alone, the layout is always drawn,
and an unstable cavity is flagged in red on it.

New ray trace panel: an offset ray and a tilted ray are pushed through
the same round-trip ABCD matrices for 1-40 round trips, in either plane,
and stopped at an adjustable aperture. The note under it gives the
round-trip Gouy phase, warns near the stability edge and near
re-entrant (degenerate) points, and gives the per-round-trip growth
factor when |m| > 1. The tangential rays are also overlaid on the
layout, reflecting at the mirror surfaces.

Pump and output arrows and labels now stay inside the canvas.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015k2UYA58Ace5jVaSrfKnkj
